<title>UK: B.Midland/Lufthansa plan codeshare flights.</title>
<headline>B.Midland/Lufthansa plan codeshare flights.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Privately-owned airline British Midland said on Thursday it would start codeshare flights with German airline Deutsche Lufthansa AG from May 26.</p>
<p>British Midland said in a statement it would inaugurate services from London Heathrow to Cologne and Bonn in Germany and onwards to Rome Fiumicino. It will be British Midland's first scheduled service into Italy.</p>
<p>It also said that talks are at an advanced between the two airlines to expand services to other destinations in the UK and Germany.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
